1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:07,615
Dan, please buy four carrots, three tomatoes,
and one cucumber. The blue list is for my
salad.

2
00:00:07,765 --> 00:00:09,129
I am ready.

3
00:00:09,279 --> 00:00:11,929
And what's the little drawing for?

4
00:00:12,079 --> 00:00:14,300
Four carrots. I've got it.

5
00:00:15,250 --> 00:00:20,610
Six potatoes, two onions, and broccoli for my
soup. Yellow is mine.

6
00:00:20,760 --> 00:00:23,040
Two colors. Two delicious plans.

7
00:00:23,190 --> 00:00:25,470
Keep mine behind Maya's, okay?

8
00:00:25,620 --> 00:00:28,340
They both fit in one hand.

9
00:00:30,250 --> 00:00:31,756
Blue for salad.

10
00:00:31,906 --> 00:00:33,411
Yellow for soup.

11
00:00:33,561 --> 00:00:37,906
I have both. My memory has plenty of room.

12
00:00:38,056 --> 00:00:42,400
There's room for the actual notes, too, I
hope.

13
00:00:45,250 --> 00:00:47,530
Should we check those together?

14
00:00:47,680 --> 00:00:49,960
I have an excellent memory.

15
00:00:50,110 --> 00:00:53,270
We can bring excellent eyes as well.

16
00:00:53,420 --> 00:00:57,460
Can my eyes come along? They're good at
broccoli.

17
00:01:00,250 --> 00:01:02,530
Blue soup, yellow salad. Easy.

18
00:01:02,680 --> 00:01:04,520
That sounds backward, Dad.

19
00:01:04,670 --> 00:01:08,710
Then we will check the details at the stall.

20
00:01:08,860 --> 00:01:12,460
I'll hold you to that. Both headings, okay?

21
00:01:15,250 --> 00:01:19,290
I will carry the bags and check the
vegetables.

22
00:01:19,440 --> 00:01:23,920
I have the basket. Does broccoli need a seat
belt?

23
00:01:24,070 --> 00:01:26,790
Only if you drive it, Max.

24
00:01:26,940 --> 00:01:29,220
I'll walk it very carefully.

25
00:01:30,250 --> 00:01:31,210
Ready, team?

26
00:01:31,360 --> 00:01:34,520
Ready. Even our empty basket looks hungry.

27
00:01:34,670 --> 00:01:39,150
Then let us bring it back with the right
lunch.

28
00:01:39,300 --> 00:01:43,340
Come on, before the basket orders its own
lunch.

29
00:01:45,250 --> 00:01:48,410
Vegetables, team. We need vegetables, not
surprises.

30
00:01:48,560 --> 00:01:51,280
The stand is on the right.

31
00:01:51,430 --> 00:01:54,150
The surprises may be there too.

32
00:01:54,300 --> 00:01:57,900
I can smell the tomatoes from here, Dad.

33
00:02:00,250 --> 00:02:04,730
Can you carry the basket, Dad? It is very
heavy.

34
00:02:04,880 --> 00:02:06,720
But it is empty!

35
00:02:06,870 --> 00:02:10,030
I am saving my muscles for later.

36
00:02:10,180 --> 00:02:14,220
Saving them for when the basket actually
weighs something?

37
00:02:15,250 --> 00:02:18,850
The bags can wait here while we choose.

38
00:02:19,000 --> 00:02:21,720
And we keep the aisle clear.

39
00:02:21,870 --> 00:02:24,150
An organized beginning. I approve.

40
00:02:24,300 --> 00:02:28,340
Wait till we put the shopping in it, Dad.

41
00:02:30,250 --> 00:02:32,530
Ours has the blue handle.

42
00:02:32,680 --> 00:02:36,280
Good. We are not shopping for somebody else.

43
00:02:36,430 --> 00:02:40,030
Let us check the food just as carefully.

44
00:02:40,180 --> 00:02:44,220
Blue handle. I'd know that squeak anywhere by
now.

45
00:02:45,250 --> 00:02:46,282
Forty carrots?

46
00:02:46,432 --> 00:02:48,411
Four, Dad. Four carrots.

47
00:02:48,561 --> 00:02:52,906
Good catch. Forty would need their own
shopping cart.

48
00:02:53,056 --> 00:02:57,400
And we'd be eating carrots well into next
week.

49
00:03:00,250 --> 00:03:02,229
One, two, three, four.

50
00:03:02,379 --> 00:03:05,304
Four is much easier to carry.

51
00:03:05,454 --> 00:03:08,852
And exactly what the list asked for.

52
00:03:09,002 --> 00:03:12,400
I'll take the ones you counted, then.

53
00:03:15,250 --> 00:03:17,970
Should we get a few extra?

54
00:03:18,120 --> 00:03:19,960
We have four already.

55
00:03:20,110 --> 00:03:23,710
Then the others can stay for another family.

56
00:03:23,860 --> 00:03:27,900
Thanks. My arms were starting to worry about
forty.

57
00:03:30,250 --> 00:03:34,290
Three ripe tomatoes. The tray will keep them
safe.

58
00:03:34,440 --> 00:03:36,280
Three tiny bowling balls?

59
00:03:36,430 --> 00:03:39,590
Only if you want tomato soup everywhere.

60
00:03:39,740 --> 00:03:43,780
Nobody bowl. I'd like these to make it home.

61
00:03:45,250 --> 00:03:47,090
Three tomatoes, safely aboard.

62
00:03:47,240 --> 00:03:49,960
Keep the heavy things underneath later.

63
00:03:50,110 --> 00:03:53,270
A first-class ticket for the soft passengers.

64
00:03:53,420 --> 00:03:57,460
Just promise you won't roll them down the
aisle.

65
00:04:00,250 --> 00:04:03,757
We can make room before anything gets
squashed.

66
00:04:03,907 --> 00:04:08,700
Good idea. The tomatoes should finish this
trip looking like tomatoes.

67
00:04:08,850 --> 00:04:11,500
Can you keep the tray level?

68
00:04:11,650 --> 00:04:14,300
Like it's carrying eggs. Got it.

69
00:04:15,250 --> 00:04:18,410
Long, green, ready for salad. A cucumber!

70
00:04:18,560 --> 00:04:23,480
That is a zucchini. The cucumbers are in the
next crate.

71
00:04:23,630 --> 00:04:25,030
A useful introduction.

72
00:04:25,180 --> 00:04:28,780
Check the little sign before you introduce
yourself.

73
00:04:30,250 --> 00:04:32,970
This is the cucumber we need.

74
00:04:33,120 --> 00:04:37,600
Two green cousins. I checked the right name
this time.

75
00:04:37,750 --> 00:04:40,030
And only one comes home.

76
00:04:40,180 --> 00:04:44,220
Lucky cucumber. The other cousin can visit
another time.

77
00:04:45,250 --> 00:04:48,410
Shape helps, but the label helps too.

78
00:04:48,560 --> 00:04:51,280
I will use both next time.

79
00:04:51,430 --> 00:04:55,030
That gives your excellent memory a little
help.

80
00:04:55,180 --> 00:04:59,220
My excellent memory appreciates a sign it can
read.

81
00:05:00,250 --> 00:05:02,970
The yellow note is still hiding.

82
00:05:03,120 --> 00:05:05,840
Then it deserves some fresh air.

83
00:05:05,990 --> 00:05:09,150
And a careful look at its heading.

84
00:05:09,300 --> 00:05:12,900
Good thing you noticed the corner peeking out.

85
00:05:15,250 --> 00:05:19,290
Six potatoes for the salad? That sounds very
crunchy.

86
00:05:19,440 --> 00:05:22,160
Maybe we should check the heading.

87
00:05:22,310 --> 00:05:25,030
Yes. Before we sort the bags.

88
00:05:25,180 --> 00:05:29,220
That's one question worth keeping till we see
both.

89
00:05:30,250 --> 00:05:33,850
Six potatoes. One, two, three, four, five,
six.

90
00:05:34,000 --> 00:05:35,400
Heavy passengers downstairs.

91
00:05:35,550 --> 00:05:38,710
And the tomatoes keep their safe seats.

92
00:05:38,860 --> 00:05:42,900
Nobody wants to sit under a sack of potatoes.

93
00:05:45,250 --> 00:05:48,549
The potatoes will not squash the tomatoes now.

94
00:05:48,699 --> 00:05:51,998
Good. At least their travel arrangements are
clear.

95
00:05:52,148 --> 00:05:55,044
We can make the lists clear too.

96
00:05:55,194 --> 00:05:59,300
Two lists, two jobs. I'll let you help me
sort.

97
00:06:00,250 --> 00:06:03,410
These onions are making me cry already.

98
00:06:03,560 --> 00:06:05,840
You have not cut them.

99
00:06:05,990 --> 00:06:08,710
Perhaps they heard my potato-salad plan.

100
00:06:08,860 --> 00:06:12,900
I'm not crying. They're still wearing all
their coats.

101
00:06:15,250 --> 00:06:18,850
One onion, two onions. Which dish gets them?

102
00:06:19,000 --> 00:06:20,400
An excellent question.

103
00:06:20,550 --> 00:06:25,030
We can ask the notes when we open them
properly.

104
00:06:25,180 --> 00:06:29,220
Remind me when we get to the bags, okay?

105
00:06:30,250 --> 00:06:34,481
We can check before anything goes in the wrong
bag.

106
00:06:34,631 --> 00:06:36,784
That is a good plan.

107
00:06:36,934 --> 00:06:40,334
There is still plenty of time to ask.

108
00:06:40,484 --> 00:06:44,300
Good. I can still get this right before lunch.

109
00:06:45,250 --> 00:06:48,410
That broccoli looks like a tiny tree.

110
00:06:48,560 --> 00:06:51,720
A forest small enough for our basket.

111
00:06:51,870 --> 00:06:55,470
Then I will save it a window seat.

112
00:06:55,620 --> 00:06:59,220
Just one tree. We're shopping for lunch,
remember?

113
00:07:00,250 --> 00:07:04,066
One head of broccoli. That is all we need.

114
00:07:04,216 --> 00:07:06,369
The forest has arrived safely.

115
00:07:06,519 --> 00:07:10,334
And the basket still has room for the rest.

116
00:07:10,484 --> 00:07:14,300
Good. I can see the bottom getting pretty
full.

117
00:07:15,250 --> 00:07:19,897
Why is it a bell pepper if it does not ring?

118
00:07:20,047 --> 00:07:22,200
Perhaps it is on silent.

119
00:07:22,350 --> 00:07:25,334
That is very polite in a shop.

120
00:07:25,484 --> 00:07:29,300
Imagine a whole crate ringing every time
someone shops.

121
00:07:30,250 --> 00:07:34,290
The blue list asks for one red bell pepper.

122
00:07:34,440 --> 00:07:38,920
Blue paper, red pepper. I will keep those
details separate.

123
00:07:39,070 --> 00:07:40,470
That will help.

124
00:07:40,620 --> 00:07:44,220
Red is the vegetable. Blue is the paper.

125
00:07:45,250 --> 00:07:49,426
That one looks good. The skin is not damaged.

126
00:07:49,576 --> 00:07:51,932
And it has excellent manners.

127
00:07:52,082 --> 00:07:53,074
Still silent?

128
00:07:53,224 --> 00:07:57,400
Quiet as ever. I think we found our pepper.

129
00:08:00,250 --> 00:08:03,205
One red bell pepper, safely packed.

130
00:08:03,355 --> 00:08:04,278
Checked.

131
00:08:04,428 --> 00:08:08,339
A quiet ingredient and a very useful helper.

132
00:08:08,489 --> 00:08:12,400
It didn't ring once. Max will be impressed.

133
00:08:15,250 --> 00:08:18,971
Two ears of corn. Can they hear us?

134
00:08:19,121 --> 00:08:21,932
Only if we speak very politely.

135
00:08:22,082 --> 00:08:23,529
Good morning, corn.

136
00:08:23,679 --> 00:08:27,400
I think they heard you from that basket.

137
00:08:30,250 --> 00:08:32,530
Two ears. Both look fresh.

138
00:08:32,680 --> 00:08:34,960
They came as a pair.

139
00:08:35,110 --> 00:08:38,710
Then let us keep their ride gentle too.

140
00:08:38,860 --> 00:08:42,900
Stalk side in, then. I like my elbows
unscratched.

141
00:08:45,250 --> 00:08:47,070
Two ears, safely aboard.

142
00:08:47,220 --> 00:08:49,039
Thank you for listening.

143
00:08:49,189 --> 00:08:51,879
They are our most patient passengers.

144
00:08:52,029 --> 00:08:55,590
They haven't interrupted a single joke all
morning.

145
00:08:55,740 --> 00:08:59,300
Then I think they deserve the nice seat.

146
00:09:00,250 --> 00:09:02,090
A very tidy lettuce?

147
00:09:02,240 --> 00:09:06,280
That is cabbage. Our list asks for loose-leaf
lettuce.

148
00:09:06,430 --> 00:09:09,590
Then we need the less tidy one.

149
00:09:09,740 --> 00:09:13,780
Look at those open leaves in the next crate.

150
00:09:15,250 --> 00:09:17,970
These leaves are loose and open.

151
00:09:18,120 --> 00:09:20,400
Not a round cabbage ball.

152
00:09:20,550 --> 00:09:23,270
Right. One lettuce for the salad.

153
00:09:23,420 --> 00:09:27,460
Now I can spot it without guessing the name.

154
00:09:30,250 --> 00:09:32,970
The lettuce gets the top seat.

155
00:09:33,120 --> 00:09:35,840
Soft leaves need a gentle journey.

156
00:09:35,990 --> 00:09:39,590
Our basket is becoming a very considerate bus.

157
00:09:39,740 --> 00:09:43,780
Save a little space up here for one more.

158
00:09:45,250 --> 00:09:46,697
One ingredient left.

159
00:09:46,847 --> 00:09:49,658
The little bag of green leaves.

160
00:09:49,808 --> 00:09:52,620
Then spinach is our final passenger.

161
00:09:52,770 --> 00:09:57,400
Do we need a whole bush or just a bag?

162
00:10:00,250 --> 00:10:02,970
Spinach. Is this the last passenger?

163
00:10:03,120 --> 00:10:05,400
Yes. One bag of spinach.

164
00:10:05,550 --> 00:10:08,710
Then the basket can stop taking reservations.

165
00:10:08,860 --> 00:10:12,900
Once that's in, we'll see what the notes say.

166
00:10:15,250 --> 00:10:18,410
That is everything. Ten ingredient lines
checked.

167
00:10:18,560 --> 00:10:20,400
All the right vegetables.

168
00:10:20,550 --> 00:10:24,590
Now we can check which dish gets which ones.

169
00:10:24,740 --> 00:10:29,220
All ten? Good. Let's lay those notes side by
side.

170
00:10:30,250 --> 00:10:34,481
Let us put them where we can see both
headings.

171
00:10:34,631 --> 00:10:36,369
Blue salad. Yellow soup.

172
00:10:36,519 --> 00:10:39,919
That is what they have said all morning.

173
00:10:40,069 --> 00:10:44,300
I see it now. I switched them in my head.

174
00:10:45,250 --> 00:10:50,021
I put the dish names in the wrong places in my
head.

175
00:10:50,171 --> 00:10:52,983
The vegetables are in the right place.

176
00:10:53,133 --> 00:10:55,554
And we can sort them correctly.

177
00:10:55,704 --> 00:10:59,300
Good thing nobody has to put the onions back.

178
00:11:00,250 --> 00:11:04,629
Maya, I remembered the colors backward. Blue
is your salad, right?

179
00:11:04,779 --> 00:11:09,941
Right. The blue list is my salad. You can
check it with me.

180
00:11:10,091 --> 00:11:12,512
So the carrots really are yours?

181
00:11:12,662 --> 00:11:14,300
Yes, all four, please.

182
00:11:15,250 --> 00:11:20,043
And yellow is my soup. Potatoes, onions,
broccoli, corn and spinach.

183
00:11:20,193 --> 00:11:25,415
The soup sounds much better now that it has
its own ingredients.

184
00:11:25,565 --> 00:11:27,357
Even the little tree?

185
00:11:27,507 --> 00:11:29,300
Especially the broccoli, Max.

186
00:11:30,250 --> 00:11:32,743
I should have asked before guessing.

187
00:11:32,893 --> 00:11:36,595
You are asking now. We are glad to help.

188
00:11:36,745 --> 00:11:40,448
Bring our vegetables and our three helpers
home safely.

189
00:11:40,598 --> 00:11:44,300
We'll bring him home too. He's learning the
route.

190
00:11:45,250 --> 00:11:49,290
Phone away. Two headings where we can see
them.

191
00:11:49,440 --> 00:11:51,720
That will make packing easier.

192
00:11:51,870 --> 00:11:55,030
And make my memory work less hard.

193
00:11:55,180 --> 00:11:59,220
The bags will do the remembering once they're
packed.

194
00:12:00,250 --> 00:12:05,162
I mixed up the lists. Thank you for catching
it before packing.

195
00:12:05,312 --> 00:12:06,998
We are a team.

196
00:12:07,148 --> 00:12:10,851
Then let us give each dish its own bag.

197
00:12:11,001 --> 00:12:14,300
I'm taking orders from the packing crew now.

198
00:12:15,250 --> 00:12:18,410
Blue bag beside the blue salad note.

199
00:12:18,560 --> 00:12:20,400
Yellow beside yellow soup.

200
00:12:20,550 --> 00:12:23,710
A filing system I can actually see.

201
00:12:23,860 --> 00:12:27,460
Keep them open so we can see inside.

202
00:12:30,250 --> 00:12:33,410
Read the heading, then match the ingredients.

203
00:12:33,560 --> 00:12:36,280
Salad in blue. Soup in yellow.

204
00:12:36,430 --> 00:12:40,470
Now we can make the bags match the notes.

205
00:12:40,620 --> 00:12:44,220
I'll say each name while you check it.

206
00:12:45,250 --> 00:12:48,850
Four carrots, three tomatoes, cucumber,
lettuce, red pepper.

207
00:12:49,000 --> 00:12:50,840
All for Maya's salad.

208
00:12:50,990 --> 00:12:53,270
The blue bag is ready.

209
00:12:53,420 --> 00:12:57,460
That one's hers. What belongs in the yellow
bag?

210
00:13:00,250 --> 00:13:04,730
Potatoes, onions, broccoli, corn and spinach.
All for Nina's soup.

211
00:13:04,880 --> 00:13:07,600
The basket has finished its job.

212
00:13:07,750 --> 00:13:09,590
An excellent passenger service.

213
00:13:09,740 --> 00:13:12,900
No passengers left under the handle, either.

214
00:13:15,250 --> 00:13:18,850
Blue salad. Yellow soup. Checked properly this
time.

215
00:13:19,000 --> 00:13:20,840
Both bags look right.

216
00:13:20,990 --> 00:13:24,150
Now we can pay for the vegetables.

217
00:13:24,300 --> 00:13:28,340
I'll keep them apart on the way to checkout.

218
00:13:30,250 --> 00:13:32,970
Eighteen dollars and fifty cents, please.

219
00:13:33,120 --> 00:13:34,080
Eighteen fifty.

220
00:13:34,230 --> 00:13:38,710
That matches our vegetables. We can check the
receipt too.

221
00:13:38,860 --> 00:13:42,460
Let me get my wallet while you look.

222
00:13:45,250 --> 00:13:47,339
Here you go. Twenty dollars.

223
00:13:47,489 --> 00:13:51,192
We should get one dollar and fifty cents back.

224
00:13:51,342 --> 00:13:55,448
Then I will check that as carefully as the
lists.

225
00:13:55,598 --> 00:13:59,300
I'll listen for the coins when they come back.

226
00:14:00,250 --> 00:14:02,090
Here is your receipt.

227
00:14:02,240 --> 00:14:04,520
All ten ingredients are here.

228
00:14:04,670 --> 00:14:09,150
Good. Right vegetables, right total, and
nearly the right memory.

229
00:14:09,300 --> 00:14:12,460
Eighteen fifty, Dad. The bottom line agrees.

230
00:14:15,250 --> 00:14:18,175
One dollar. Two quarters. One fifty.

231
00:14:18,325 --> 00:14:20,304
Small change, carefully checked.

232
00:14:20,454 --> 00:14:22,906
The smallest passengers still count.

233
00:14:23,056 --> 00:14:27,400
Good thing those quarters don't roll around
the basket.

234
00:14:30,250 --> 00:14:32,530
Receipt and change, both checked.

235
00:14:32,680 --> 00:14:34,960
And safely in my wallet.

236
00:14:35,110 --> 00:14:40,030
That is a better place for them than under the
lettuce.

237
00:14:40,180 --> 00:14:44,220
Lettuce is terrible at keeping track of small
change.

238
00:14:45,250 --> 00:14:46,650
Nothing left behind.

239
00:14:46,800 --> 00:14:49,960
Except the vegetables we did not buy.

240
00:14:50,110 --> 00:14:54,590
They can stay. We have exactly what our family
needs.

241
00:14:54,740 --> 00:14:58,780
One last look around our feet, then we're off.

242
00:15:00,250 --> 00:15:02,530
All three helpers. Both bags.

243
00:15:02,680 --> 00:15:04,960
And one safely empty basket.

244
00:15:05,110 --> 00:15:08,710
It worked very hard without learning to cook.

245
00:15:08,860 --> 00:15:12,900
Neither did I. We'll need help in the kitchen.

246
00:15:15,250 --> 00:15:18,850
Maya, your salad vegetables. Blue bag, blue
list.

247
00:15:19,000 --> 00:15:20,400
And our helpers?

248
00:15:20,550 --> 00:15:23,710
All three. We checked that part too.

249
00:15:23,860 --> 00:15:27,900
I see my carrots. Who kept the tomatoes safe?

250
00:15:30,250 --> 00:15:34,290
My soup vegetables! Did the broccoli enjoy its
trip?

251
00:15:34,440 --> 00:15:37,160
It asked for a window seat.

252
00:15:37,310 --> 00:15:39,590
We offered very careful service.

253
00:15:39,740 --> 00:15:44,220
Then it can travel the last few feet with me.

254
00:15:45,250 --> 00:15:47,043
Exactly what we needed.

255
00:15:47,193 --> 00:15:50,700
And a funny story to go with it.

256
00:15:50,850 --> 00:15:55,214
I would like the next part to involve fewer
guesses.

257
00:15:55,364 --> 00:15:59,300
Can the tiny tree be in my bowl later?

258
00:16:00,250 --> 00:16:02,530
Hands first, after our trip.

259
00:16:02,680 --> 00:16:06,280
Then we can help with the safe jobs.

260
00:16:06,430 --> 00:16:09,590
Yes. Everybody has a part in lunch.

261
00:16:09,740 --> 00:16:13,340
Can my elbows have the afternoon off, though?

262
00:16:15,250 --> 00:16:18,410
Even our well-traveled cucumber gets a wash.

263
00:16:18,560 --> 00:16:19,960
Especially that cucumber.

264
00:16:20,110 --> 00:16:25,470
Then the adults can do the cutting while you
set the table.

265
00:16:25,620 --> 00:16:29,220
I can do that while the cucumber dries.

266
00:16:30,250 --> 00:16:33,146
I will take care of the napkins.

267
00:16:33,296 --> 00:16:36,192
And I will help with the vegetables.

268
00:16:36,342 --> 00:16:40,448
Careful hands and clear jobs. This part is
coming together.

269
00:16:40,598 --> 00:16:44,300
I'll leave you a clear spot to work, Dad.

270
00:16:45,250 --> 00:16:46,988
Shopping finished. Lunch finished?

271
00:16:47,138 --> 00:16:50,953
We brought ingredients, Dan. They have not
cooked themselves.

272
00:16:51,103 --> 00:16:55,750
Then I am glad we left time for the next job.

273
00:16:55,900 --> 00:16:59,300
You'll smell the difference when it's actually
ready.

274
00:17:00,250 --> 00:17:02,090
The salad is ready.

275
00:17:02,240 --> 00:17:05,400
And now the soup is cooked, too.

276
00:17:05,550 --> 00:17:10,030
Two dishes. One kitchen that has done some
excellent work.

277
00:17:10,180 --> 00:17:13,780
And everybody will taste what you brought
home.

278
00:17:15,250 --> 00:17:17,530
Six places. Everybody has one.

279
00:17:17,680 --> 00:17:19,520
Even the smallest helper.

280
00:17:19,670 --> 00:17:25,030
Especially the smallest helper. And the basket
can rest on its chair.

281
00:17:25,180 --> 00:17:28,780
I don't think it's hungry after that trip.

282
00:17:30,250 --> 00:17:31,650
Salad for everyone.

283
00:17:31,800 --> 00:17:36,280
And cooked soup. Let it cool enough before you
taste.

284
00:17:36,430 --> 00:17:40,030
Lunch has finally arrived at the right seats.

285
00:17:40,180 --> 00:17:44,220
Mine smells good from all the way over here.

286
00:17:45,250 --> 00:17:49,897
I felt embarrassed when I realized I mixed up
the lists.

287
00:17:50,047 --> 00:17:55,109
We helped because we love you. You help us
learn every day.

288
00:17:55,259 --> 00:17:57,828
Even when I get something backward?

289
00:17:57,978 --> 00:17:59,300
Especially then, Dad.

290
00:18:00,250 --> 00:18:02,970
You listened, checked, and tried again.

291
00:18:03,120 --> 00:18:06,280
And all our ingredients found their dishes.

292
00:18:06,430 --> 00:18:10,030
I had very good company along the way.

293
00:18:10,180 --> 00:18:14,220
And guess who gets to try both dishes today?

294
00:18:15,250 --> 00:18:18,850
Would forty carrots need their own dining
table?

295
00:18:19,000 --> 00:18:21,720
Only if they came as guests.

296
00:18:21,870 --> 00:18:25,030
Then four was a very considerate number.

297
00:18:25,180 --> 00:18:28,780
Four guests are much easier to squeeze in.

298
00:18:30,250 --> 00:18:33,410
A question helped more than another guess.

299
00:18:33,560 --> 00:18:36,280
Especially when the vegetables had ears.

300
00:18:36,430 --> 00:18:39,590
That was the polite part of shopping.

301
00:18:39,740 --> 00:18:43,340
I still think the corn understood good
morning.

302
00:18:45,250 --> 00:18:49,237
Next time I am unsure, could you check with
me?

303
00:18:49,387 --> 00:18:52,983
Of course. Asking for help is always welcome
here.

304
00:18:53,133 --> 00:18:55,554
That sounds like a useful plan.

305
00:18:55,704 --> 00:18:59,300
I'd rather hear your question while there's
still time.

306
00:19:00,250 --> 00:19:01,210
Blue salad.

307
00:19:01,360 --> 00:19:02,320
Yellow soup.

308
00:19:02,470 --> 00:19:08,270
Two notes that deserve to be read separately.
I will remember that part.

309
00:19:08,420 --> 00:19:12,460
We'll bring our excellent eyes along next time
too.

310
00:19:15,250 --> 00:19:18,719
Tomorrow, we need fruit for a picnic.

311
00:19:18,869 --> 00:19:20,406
One list, please.

312
00:19:20,556 --> 00:19:22,577
One list. Two colors.

313
00:19:22,727 --> 00:19:23,781
You're kidding.

314
00:19:23,931 --> 00:19:27,400
Wait till you see what we're buying.

315
00:19:30,250 --> 00:19:32,970
Tomorrow, we can choose fruit together.

316
00:19:33,120 --> 00:19:36,720
Three excellent helpers, and all six of us.

317
00:19:36,870 --> 00:19:40,030
That sounds like a very good team.

318
00:19:40,180 --> 00:19:43,780
Leo can count while Max interviews the fruit.

319
00:19:45,250 --> 00:19:47,530
Two dishes. One happy family.

320
00:19:47,680 --> 00:19:49,960
Exactly the plan we wanted.

321
00:19:50,110 --> 00:19:53,710
And nobody left the basket at the market.

322
00:19:53,860 --> 00:19:57,900
Let's finish lunch before that basket gets
another job.
